---
// src/pages/accessibility.astro
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Accessibility Statement | PSFF Season 03">
  <article
    class="w-full border-b border-zinc-900 py-16 sm:py-24 px-6 sm:px-12 selection:bg-[#D9381E] selection:text-[#F6F4EE]"
  >
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-12 sm:space-y-16">
      <!-- Page Header -->
      <header class="space-y-4 border-b border-zinc-300 pb-8">
        <div
          class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-zinc-500 flex items-center gap-2"
        >
          <a href="/" class="hover:text-[#D9381E] transition-colors"
            >&larr; Home</a
          >
          <span>/</span>
          <span>Accessibility</span>
        </div>

        <h1
          class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-black uppercase tracking-tight text-[#161616] leading-none"
        >
          Accessibility Statement
        </h1>

        <p
          class="font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm text-[#D9381E] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider"
        >
          Pazhassi Short Film Festival &bull; Web &amp; Physical Venue Access
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- Main Content -->
      <div
        class="space-y-10 font-serif text-lg sm:text-xl text-zinc-800 leading-relaxed sm:leading-loose"
      >
        <p
          class="first-letter:text-6xl first-letter:font-black first-letter:float-left first-letter:mr-4 first-letter:leading-none first-letter:text-[#161616]"
        >
          The Pazhassi Short Film Festival (PSFF), organized by Drishtidosham
          Chalachithravedi and Pazhassi Raja Smaraka Granthalayam, is committed
          to making our festival screenings, physical venues, and digital
          platforms as inclusive and accessible as possible for filmmakers,
          jurors, and audience members.
        </p>

        <div class="space-y-4">
          <h2
            class="font-mono text-base sm:text-lg font-black uppercase text-[#161616] border-b-2 border-[#161616] pb-1"
          >
            1. Digital Portal &amp; Web Accessibility
          </h2>
          <p class="text-base sm:text-lg">
            Our submission portal, evaluation workspace, and official website
            are built following web accessibility standards (WCAG 2.1
            principles):
          </p>
          <ul
            class="font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm space-y-2 list-disc list-inside text-zinc-700"
          >
            <li>
              <strong>High-Contrast Typography:</strong> High-contrast color pairings
              across UI elements and text blocks for clear readability.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Semantic HTML Architecture:</strong> Proper heading hierarchies,
              structured tables, landmark regions, and form labels to support assistive
              technologies.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Keyboard Navigable:</strong> Complete keyboard accessibility
              for submitting entry forms, modal dialogs, and rubric scoring interfaces.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Responsive Layouts:</strong> Scalable viewports and fluid sizing
              that function cleanly across mobile devices, tablets, and desktop displays
              without loss of content.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-4">
          <h2
            class="font-mono text-base sm:text-lg font-black uppercase text-[#161616] border-b-2 border-[#161616] pb-1"
          >
            2. Film Screenings &amp; Subtitles
          </h2>
          <p class="text-base sm:text-lg">
            To ensure non-Malayalam speakers, jury members, and individuals who
            are deaf or hard of hearing can fully engage with competition
            entries:
          </p>
          <ul
            class="font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm space-y-2 list-disc list-inside text-zinc-700"
          >
            <li>
              All non-English language submissions are required to include
              clear, legible English subtitles for both preliminary screening
              and festival theater projection.
            </li>
            <li>
              Burned-in or embedded closed-caption tracks are accepted and
              encouraged during registration.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-4">
          <h2
            class="font-mono text-base sm:text-lg font-black uppercase text-[#161616] border-b-2 border-[#161616] pb-1"
          >
            3. Physical Festival Venue
          </h2>
          <p class="text-base sm:text-lg">
            Festival public screenings take place at <strong
              >Veena - Varna Theatre, Mananthavady</strong
            >:
          </p>
          <ul
            class="font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm space-y-2 list-disc list-inside text-zinc-700"
          >
            <li>
              Ground-level entry points and wheelchair-accessible seating
              options are available inside the cinema auditorium.
            </li>
            <li>
              Our volunteer reception team will be present at the theater
              entrance to assist visitors requiring mobility support, reserved
              seating, or special assistance.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-4">
          <h2
            class="font-mono text-base sm:text-lg font-black uppercase text-[#161616] border-b-2 border-[#161616] pb-1"
          >
            4. Feedback &amp; Assistance
          </h2>
          <p class="text-base sm:text-lg">
            We actively work to improve accessibility across all festival
            touchpoints. If you encounter any digital barrier, have questions
            regarding venue access, or require specific accommodations during
            the festival, please reach out to our organizing team at <a
              href="mailto:convener@psff.in"
              class="text-[#D9381E] font-bold underline underline-offset-4"
              >convener@psff.in</a
            >.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
